    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2057754485083050062",
      "url": "https://x.com/Bamboo_Web3/status/2057754485083050062",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Bamboo_Web3/status/2057754485083050062",
      "text": "There is a price for everything.\n\nCoffee. Cocoa. Sugar. Beef. \n\nThe things that feed the world, fuel economies, and sit at the center of trade routes that have existed for centuries.\n\nBut ask a Web3 builder to access those prices onchain six months ago and they would laugh at you. \n\nOr cry.\n\nDepends on the builder.\n\nThat gap always bothered me.\nBecause I know what it means when a developer in Lagos or Manila or Nairobi cannot build around the prices that actually move their local economy.\n\nIt means the tools keep getting built for someone else. Again.\n\nThe same someone else. Every time.\n\nThen @PythNetwork moved.\n\nFour new feeds.\nCocoa.\nCoffee.\nRaw Sugar.\nLive Cattle.\n\nQuietly dropped into the Pyth Pro catalog like it was nothing, but if you understand what that actually means, you stopped scrolling.\n\nThese are not random assets.\n\nThese are the commodities that dominate trade across Africa, Southeast Asia, and Latin America.\n\nThe crops people plant, harvest, and pray over. The livestock entire regional economies are built around.\n\nAnd now their prices are live, real, institutional grade and are also accessible onchain. \n\nAccessible to anyone.\nNo Bloomberg terminal.\nNo legacy vendor contract.\nNo toll booth.\n\nJust the price.\nClean.\nAvailable.\nProgrammable.\n\nPyth sits at 3,000+ feeds now. Crypto, equities, FX, metals, energy, and now the soft commodities and livestock that the rest of DeFi forgot existed.\n\nAll under one API.\nOne subscription.\nhttps://t.co/8rEjuyiMNW\n\nThe timing is not an accident either.\n\nTariffs are rewriting trade routes. Climate is hitting harvests in ways the models did not predict.\n\nSupply chains that everyone assumed were stable are showing just how fragile they always were. In that environment, soft commodities and livestock are some of the most actively traded contracts on the planet.\n\nAnd builders in Web3 can now touch them.\n\nPrediction markets priced in cocoa. Perpetual exchanges running on coffee futures. Structured products built around cattle; the same way others build around BTC.\n\nThe infrastructure is here.\n\nThe only question is who builds first.\n\nThat is the invitation sitting inside this announcement.\n\nThe price of everything is coming onchain.\n\nOne feed at a time.💡",
